# The prover every proof results file cites. One line per field, `key value`.
# tools/tlapm refuses a binary whose sha256 is not binary_sha256 unless TLAPM_UNPINNED=1 is set;
# tools/install-tlaps.sh compares what it installed with this file; scripts/proof_sync.py compares
# the prover each proof results file prints with it.
# This is the build the tla-kit image carries (tools/TLA-KIT-PIN tlapm_sha256), so CI regenerates
# the proof results files in the image and compares them in full. Upstream's 1.6.0-pre tag is
# rebuilt under the same name, so the tarball is fetched from tla-kit's kept copy (url), a release
# that is never moved. The pin came here from c8ddc44 on 2026.11.17, when that build was no longer
# served anywhere; the move needed one step of Government_proof.tla split (ShapeNamedPaths <1>2).
